# Two native suites share one test binary, and one of them has a block that
# fails an assertion and a block that a signal kills.
#
# A failed assertion and a death each end the process running them, and the
# blocks of a suite share processes. **Every other block still runs and keeps
# its own verdict**: the blocks around the two that end a process pass and are
# reported as passing, the two are named, and the suite beside them is not
# touched. The report is the one each suite would get alone.
#
# The negative twin is the base case: with it the recursion returns, and only
# the assertion fails.
#
# Schema: the repository-case manifest, cli/tests/harness/case.rs. Textproto,
# but not a Buri file: only repo/ below is a Buri repository.

doc: "a block that fails or kills its process in a shared test binary is the block the report names, and every other block keeps its verdict"

# The report names the signal, and a stack overflow is a different one on each
# host: SIGBUS on macOS, SIGSEGV on Linux.
run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/...", "--force"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "died.txt"
  host: MACOS
}

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/...", "--force"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "died-linux.txt"
  host: LINUX
}

# The negative twin: a base case, and only the assertion fails.
edit {
  file: "lib/deep/deep.buri"
  replace: "if (n == 0) { 0 } else { deep(n + 1) + 1 }"
  with: "if (n == 0) { 0 } else { deep(n - 1) + 1 }"
}

run {
  args: ["test", "//lib/...", "--force"]
  exit: 1
  golden: "failed.txt"
}
